 79   Policy
 80       The Audit and Accountability (AU) control family is essential for tracking and monitoring activities
 81       within Dispel’s information systems. By generating, protecting, and retaining audit records, we
 82       ensure accountability and support investigations. These controls enable us to detect and respond to
 83       security incidents, comply with policies, and provide necessary evidence for disputes or legal
 84       actions. Implementing AU controls is crucial for maintaining the integrity and security of our
 85       systems, managing risks, and protecting sensitive information, thereby ensuring compliance with
 86       federal regulations and fostering trust in our information security practices.
 87

 88   Background
 89       The Audit and Accountability (AU) control family is part of the NIST Special Publication 800-53,
 90       which provides a catalog of security and privacy controls for federal information systems and
 91       organizations. These controls are designed to protect the confidentiality, integrity, and availability
 92       of information systems. The AU controls specifically focus on the creation, protection, and retention
 93       of audit records to ensure that activities within the system can be accurately tracked and monitored.
 94       This is critical for detecting and responding to security incidents, ensuring compliance with
 95       organizational policies, and providing evidence for investigations and legal proceedings. By
 96       implementing these controls, organizations can enhance their security posture and maintain trust in
 97       their information security practices.

 98   Purpose
 99       NIST 800-53 Field: AU-1
100       This policy and procedures document covers the purpose, scope, roles, responsibilities, management
101       commitment, coordination among organizational entities, and compliance for Dispel with respect to
102       the audit and accountability of the Dispel organization’s controls.

